- **Musculoskeletal:** No acute tenderness or swelling noted. The patient reports decreased flexion and extension of the lower back. There is no pain to palpation of the lumbar spine. Positive straight leg raise.
- **Neurological:** Motor strength is equal bilaterally. Sensation is intact in all extremities.
